  "goodToKnow": "Die Besatzung has two meanings: the crew of a ship, plane or spacecraft, and a military occupation. After 1945, Germany was divided into four Besatzungszonen (American, British, French and Soviet), a term every German pupil knows from history lessons. The occupying power is die Besatzungsmacht. For a plane, the everyday word is die Crew or die Flugbesatzung. Besetzen is the verb."
